KNOWNBUG
assignment-to-indexed-part-select-of-array-element1.sv
--bound 0
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^file .* line \d+: unsupported lvalue for RTL construction: `verilog_indexed_part_select_plus'$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
verilog_rtl_buildert::lower_lhs (src/verilog/verilog_rtl.cpp) handles
ID_symbol, ID_verilog_bit_select, ID_member and ID_typecast lvalues, but
has no case for ID_verilog_indexed_part_select_plus (or _minus). An
indexed part-select on a plain vector is accepted (it is turned into a
bit-select internally before reaching lower_lhs), but the same construct
on an array element, as in a byte-enabled memory write, is not.
